# OrbMap

OrbMap is an experimental map-based memory product for recording **sound and images in place**.

Users can capture a photo and a sound at a specific location.  
The image is transformed into an abstract animated **orb**, while the sound is preserved as part of that location-based memory.

Instead of displaying memories as conventional photo pins, OrbMap explores a more emotional and abstract way of representing personal experiences on a map.

## Product Concept

Each location can contain:
- an image
- a sound recording
- an abstract animated orb generated from the image

The orb acts as a visual representation of the memory rather than a direct reproduction of the original photo.

## Current Progress

Completed:
- Image input
- Image-to-orb visual transformation
- Dynamic orb generation prototype

In progress:
- Sound recording
- Location-based memory storage
- Map interaction
- Playback and memory browsing

## Role

Product concept, interaction design, visual system and SwiftUI prototyping.

## Status

Work in progress.
